  "goodToKnow": "Der Zimmermann is a carpenter who builds with timber: roofs, frames, half-timbered houses. Furniture is made by der Tischler or Schreiner. The plural is die Zimmerleute. Zimmer once meant timber, so a Zimmer was a timber-built room. Some young Zimmerleute still go auf die Walz: three years and a day travelling, in black corduroy outfits, working for food and board, and not allowed within 50 km of home."
